subject: security(version/update): add defense-in-depth auth to prevent unauthenticated RCE

The /api/version/update endpoint had no authentication in the handler itself,
relying solely on middleware (ALWAYS_PROTECTED in dashboardGuard). If middleware
was bypassed or misconfigured, any network-reachable client could trigger
killAppProcesses() + spawnUpdaterAndExit() — a remote code execution + DoS vector.

Fix: require either CLI machine-id token (x-9r-cli-token) OR dashboard JWT
cookie (auth_token) before executing. Optional UPDATE_SECRET env var provides
second factor when configured. Uses timing-safe comparisons to prevent
side-channel attacks.

Follows the exact pattern from src/app/api/shutdown/route.js.

Tests: 6 unit tests covering auth gate, JWT path, CLI token path, UPDATE_SECRET
enforcement, and production-only restriction. All passing.

Fixes: GAP-P0-11

